  "slug": "splice-benchmark-6b82",
  "summary": "Reproducible MFASS benchmarking and a new ensemble predictor expose shared failures of splice-disruption tools on exonic and intronic variants.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is systematic evaluation of machine-learning predictors of splicing and variant pathogenicity against experimental or clinical ground truth. A reproducible MFASS benchmark of four splice-disruption predictors on 27,733 SNVs identifies a shared exon-interior blind spot affecting 19% of disrupting variants. MetaSplice responds with a gradient-boosted ensemble combining SpliceTransformer, Pangolin, and conservation features to rank intronic SNVs, and reports outperformance. Related items apply the same evaluation logic elsewhere: an openly licensed benchmark of 49 missense predictors shows oncogenic gain-of-function variants are under-scored, with a per-gene calibration map; scOPE transfers driver-associated expression axes from bulk tumors to single cells with a ground-truth-free confidence score; Evo 2 variant severity scores correlated with TCGA radiomics yield 46 new renal cancer gene associations. The new element is explicit diagnosis of where predictors fail, not only aggregate accuracy.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-28"
}
